records='''<section class="section" id="notes-and-documents"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Notes and documents</span><h2>The details you need<br>when it matters.</h2><p class="lead">Write a private note or import a document, and keep it encrypted on your phone, with no account.</p></div><div class="steps"><div><h3>Letters and records.</h3><p>Medical letters, test results, prescriptions and appointment details, together in a place only you can open.</p></div><div><h3>Everyday paperwork.</h3><p>Insurance and policy numbers, tenancy and contract copies, and scans of a passport or ID.</p></div><div><h3>Small facts, close at hand.</h3><p>Allergies, medication lists, reference numbers and other short notes you want private but findable.</p></div></div><p class="note">Photos and notes open inside NullKey. PDFs, videos and other files are stored encrypted, and you open them by exporting a readable copy, which sits outside the vault’s protection. NullKey is not a medical record system and makes no claim about healthcare rules. Keep another copy of anything you cannot replace.</p></section>'''
