security_home='''<section class="section split"><div><span class="eyebrow">Private from us, too</span><h2>We don’t keep<br>a spare key.</h2><p class="lead">Your passphrase and recovery key unlock your vault. Alvento receives neither your vault contents nor its decryption keys.</p><a class="text-link" href="/security/">Read the security model</a></div><div class="detail-list"><div><h3>Local encryption.</h3><p>AES-256-GCM protects stored contents. Argon2id derives a key from your passphrase. The current app has no internet permission.</p></div><div><h3>Your choice of unlock.</h3><p>Use your passphrase, or enable supported biometric, phone screen-lock or in-app pattern unlock. A pattern is a convenience, with weaker protection.</p></div><div><h3>A backup you can check.</h3><p>NullKey checks the exported archive, encrypted items and thumbnails against your vault. Restore into an empty vault with the backup’s passphrase or recovery key.</p></div></div></section>'''
pricing='''<section class="section pricing" id="pricing"><div><span class="eyebrow">A clear price</span><h2>Free to start.<br>Pay once to keep going.</h2><p class="lead">Keep up to 30 photos, files and notes free. Pay once for no limit, with no subscription.</p></div><div><h3>One payment. No subscription.</h3><p>NullKey Unlimited is an optional one-time purchase in Google Play that removes the 30-item free limit. Existing items, editing, export, backup and restore stay free, whether or not you buy.</p><p>Google Play shows the final price and terms for your country before you pay, and handles refunds.</p><a href="/availability/#pricing">Read the pricing details</a></div></section>'''
faqs=faq('Can I download NullKey now?','Yes. <a href="'+PLAY+'">Get NullKey on Google Play</a>. Android 12L or later is required.')+faq('Can Alvento read my private files?','The app sends no vault contents or decryption keys to Alvento. Your phone decrypts them when you unlock. A compromised or unlocked phone remains a risk.')+faq('What if I forget my passphrase?','A saved recovery key can open an existing vault. If the phone or files are gone, you also need a backup. Losing both secrets means we cannot reset your access.')+faq('Does importing delete the originals?','No, not by default. Optional original removal checks eligible local files first. Android asks before supported photos and videos go to trash; other supported documents may be deleted permanently. Other copies can remain.')+faq('Which phones does it work on?','NullKey requires Android 12L or later. Biometric and hardware-backed unlock options depend on the device. The app has no in-app video or PDF viewer; readable exports open outside the vault’s protection.')+faq('What can I keep in notes and documents?','Anything you would rather not leave in your gallery or a general notes app: medical letters and test results, insurance and policy details, contract copies, ID scans and short private notes. Notes and photos open inside NullKey. Other files are stored encrypted, and you open them by exporting a readable copy. NullKey is not a medical record system, so keep another copy of anything you cannot replace.')
